{"id":"switch-pro-usb","name":"Nintendo Switch Pro Controller (USB)","vendor":"Nintendo","vid":"0x057E","pid":"0x2009","productString":"Pro Controller","manufacturerString":"Nintendo Co., Ltd.","type":"gamepad","connection":"usb","versionNumber":528,"descriptor":"","notes":"A Pro Controller on USB: the 203-byte report descriptor a real pad serves over USB (ControllersInfo bfc11b8, switchpro_hid_report_descriptor.bin), which switch-pro carried through v1.3.20. It declares inputs 0x21, 0x30 and 0x81 and outputs 0x01, 0x10, 0x80 and 0x82, each 63 bytes after the ID, and no 0x3F. A host starts it with the 0x80 commands (dekuNukem USB-HID-Notes.md, SDL_hidapi_switch.c BTrySetupUSB): 80 01 answers 81 01 00 03 and the MAC least significant byte first, 80 02 and 80 03 answer 81 02 and 81 03, the rest nothing. Subcommands on 0x01 answer as on Bluetooth, in 64-byte 0x21 replies whose first 49 bytes are the Bluetooth reply's. Once a host has spoken the protocol the pad sends the 64-byte 0x30 report every 15 ms, the community figure hid-nintendo quotes for a Pro Controller on USB, with bytes 49 to 63 zero, since no source gives them. It never sends 0x3F: its descriptor declares none, and SDL notes that simple mode over USB stops input reports. Rumble is decoders.rumble, raised on OutputDecoded as leftMotor and rightMotor.","layout":{"kind":"gamepad","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nintendo_Switch_Pro_Controller","sticks":[{"side":"left","xAxis":"X","yAxis":"Y","clickButton":10},{"side":"right","xAxis":"Z","yAxis":"Rz","clickButton":11}],"triggers":[],"dpad":{"encoding":"hat","hatAxis":"Hat","hatPositions":8},"faceButtons":[{"role":"face_b","buttonIndex":0},{"role":"face_a","buttonIndex":1},{"role":"face_y","buttonIndex":2},{"role":"face_x","buttonIndex":3}],"shoulderButtons":[{"role":"left_bumper","buttonIndex":4},{"role":"right_bumper","buttonIndex":5},{"role":"left_trigger_click","buttonIndex":6},{"role":"right_trigger_click","buttonIndex":7}],"systemButtons":[{"role"